hadiths[count]{hadithnumber,text}:
"2748","Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Amr bin Al-Aas, may Allah be pleased with him, said: The Messenger of Allah, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: \"He who remains silent is saved.\""
"2749","On the authority of Sayyidina Abu Huraira (RA): The Prophet (PBUH) was asked what is backbiting? He said: \"Backbiting is that you mention your brother in a way that displeases him.\" It was asked: If my brother has that defect? The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: \"If there is a defect in what you are saying, then you have backbited him, and if there is no defect in him, then you have slandered him.\""
"2750","Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Masoud (may Allah be pleased with him) narrated from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) that bad copyists are those who copy lies, and falsehood is not permissible under any circumstances, seriousness or joking, and a man should not make a false promise to his son that he cannot fulfill. And a liar is said to have lied and committed debauchery (i.e. to lie and to adopt the path of debauchery), and a person continues to speak the truth until the truth is recorded (saadiq) in the sight of Allah, and he continues to speak a lie until the liar (false) is recorded in the sight of Allah. What is it? It is the slander that causes mischief among people."
"2751","Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Amr bin Al-Aas, may Allah be pleased with him, narrated that the Messenger of Allah, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: \"A Muslim is one from whose tongue and hands other Muslims are safe.\""
"2752","Sayyiduna Abu Huraira (RA) said: The Messenger of Allah (PBUH) said: \"O people! Allah is pure and accepts pure wealth, and Allah has given the believers the same order as He gave the Messengers. Allah said: \"O Messenger! Eat pure things and do good deeds. I know what you do.\" (Al-Mu'minun 51/23) He also said: \"O believers! Eat the pure things that We have given you, and Allah.\" Give thanks to Him if you worship Him in particular (Al-Baqarah: 172/2).” The narrator said: Then the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) mentioned such a man \"who travels for a long time with scattered hair full of dust and then raises his hands to the sky and says: O Lord, O Lord, even though his food is forbidden, his clothes are forbidden, his drink is forbidden, and only forbidden food is given to him, then how will his supplication be accepted?\""
"2753","Sayyiduna Burida Aslami (RA) said: The Messenger of Allah (PBUH) said: \"A servant and a ride are enough for any of you in this world.\""
"2754","Sayyidna Mardas Aslami (RA) said: The Messenger of Allah (PBUH) said: \"The good (good) people will pass away one after the other, and after them there will be people like barley straw.\""
"2755","On the authority of Sayyidina Abu Huraira, may Allah be pleased with him, the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: \"How many are those who fast who do not get any reward for fasting, they remain (hungry) thirsty, and how many are those who worship at night that there is no benefit to their fasting except to wake up.\""
"2756","On the authority of Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Amr, may Allah be pleased with him: The Prophet, peace and blessings be upon him, mentioned prayer one day and said: \"Whoever observes it (prayer) will be a source of light and evidence and deliverance from hell on the Day of Resurrection, and whoever does not observe these prayers will neither be light nor evidence nor deliverance, but he will be with Qarun, Pharaoh, Haman and Abi bin Khalaf on the Day of Judgment.\" (Who were the worst human beings and Hellfire)."
"2757","It was narrated on the authority of Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Abbas (may Allah be pleased with him) that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to encourage the night prayer (Tahjud) until he (peace be upon him) said: \"Pray even one rak'ah at night.\""
"2758","Sayyidna Huzaifah (may God be pleased with him) said: My tongue was unrestrained towards my family members (who used to use my tongue to get drunk) but did not speak ill of anyone other than them. Sayyiduna Huzaifa said: I asked the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) about this (regretfully), and he (peace be upon him) said: \"Where are you from asking for forgiveness? That is, why do you not ask for forgiveness? I myself seek forgiveness from Allah Almighty a hundred times a day.\" \n Abu Ishaq said: I narrated this hadith to Sayyidna Abu Burda and Sayyidna Abu Bakr Ibni Abi Musa, may God be pleased with them, and they both said: The Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: \"Every day I seek forgiveness from Allah a hundred times and say: ``Astagfir Allah and repent to Him.''\""
"2759","It was narrated on the authority of Anas that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) recited this verse: “He is the People of the Pious and the People of the Forgiving” (Mutadasir: 56/74) Then he said: “Your Lord said: I am worthy to be feared and whoever fears Me, I am worthy to forgive him.”"
"2760","Sayyiduna Abu Dharr, may Allah be pleased with him, said: The Messenger of Allah, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: \"I know one such verse, if people follow it, it will be sufficient for them: \"And whoever fears Allah, He will make a way out for him\" (Al-Talaq: 2/65)."
"2761","Umm al-Mu'minin Sayyida Aisha (RA) said: The Messenger of Allah (PBUH) said to me: \"O Aisha! Save yourself from the smallest sin, Allah Ta'ala will demand of them.\""
"2762","Sayyiduna Anas (may Allah be pleased with him) said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: \"All men are sinners, and the best of sinners are those who repent.\""
"2763","Sayyidna Nu'man bin Bashir (may Allah be pleased with him) says: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: \"A man went on a journey with a camel to the desert forest. He was sleeping under the shade of a tree. His horse was also with him, on which his son and food were loaded. When he woke up, he saw that his camel had gone. He climbed a hill and nothing was seen. He climbed another hill and nothing was seen from there.\" (i.e., a camel etc.), nothing was seen from there. He turned aside and saw a camel. At that time, he must not have been as pleased as Allah is pleased with the repentance of his servant."
"2764","Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Masoud (may Allah be pleased with him) said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) made a square (square map) and drew a letter in the middle of it and drew letters around it and drew a letter that protruded from the square. When it is done, another comes and the man dies, and the letter that comes out is hope and longing."
"2765","Ka'b bin Malik narrated on the authority of his father (Sayyidna Malik Ansari, may God be pleased with him): He said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: \"If two hungry wolves are left among the goats, they will not cause as much mischief as greed for wealth and power corrupts a man's religion.\""
"2766","On the authority of Sayyidna Wathla bin Asqa, may Allah be pleased with him, the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: \"Allah the Exalted has said: I am close to the good faith of man, so let him think of me as he wishes.\""
"2767","Sayyiduna Abu Huraira, may God be pleased with him, said: When Allah revealed this verse: \"And warn your close relatives\" (Poetry: 214/26), the Prophet, may God's prayers and peace be upon him, said: \"O people of Quraysh! Buy your lives from Allah (in exchange for righteous deeds).\""
"2768","Sayyiduna Jabir, may Allah be pleased with him, said: The Messenger of Allah, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: \"Stay close to Allah and be moderate (i.e. do what you do well, do not be short or excessive) and remember that none of you will enter Paradise because of his actions.\" He said: O Messenger of Allah! Don't you too? He said: \"Neither am I except that Allah covers me in the shade of His mercy and grace.\""
"2769","Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Masoud (RA) said: The Messenger of Allah (PBUH) said: \"There is not one of you but a Satan (Jinn) has been appointed with him, his companion who lives near and a companion from among the angels.\" The Companions asked: Is it the same with you or the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)? He said: \"Yes, Satan is also with me, but Allah has helped me against him and he has become obedient to me or I have been protected from him.\" \n Imam Muhammad Darmi, may God have mercy on him, said: He has said Islam, which means he has submitted to the command."
"2770","On the authority of Anas, may Allah be pleased with him: The Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: \"If you knew what I know, you would laugh less and cry more.\""
"2771","It is narrated from Sayyiduna Anas (may Allah be pleased with him) in this chain of transmission."
"2772","It was narrated on the authority of Sayyidina Abu Huraira that the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, passed by an itchy goat kid that had been thrown out by its owner. He said: \"Do you know how worthless it is to its owner?\" He said: Yes, he said: \"By Allah, the world is more humiliated in the sight of Allah than this child is in the sight of its owner.\""
"2773","Sayyiduna Abu Dharr (may God be pleased with him) said: A companion asked the Prophet (peace be upon him): Which action is best? He said: \"To believe in Allah, then to fight in the way of Allah.\""
"2774","Sayyiduna Abu Huraira (may Allah be pleased with him) says that the Messenger of Allah (may peace be upon him) said: \"The best deed in the sight of Allah is faith; there is no doubt about it.\""
"2775","Sayyiduna Anas (may Allah be pleased with him) said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: \"None of you will be a believer unless he wishes for his brother what he wishes for himself.\""
"2776","It was narrated from Anas (may Allah be pleased with him) that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: \"None of you will be a believer until I become more beloved to him than his father, his children and all people.\""
"2777","On the authority of Sayyidina Abu Bakrah, a companion said: O Messenger of Allah! Who is the best in logos? He said: \"Whoever has a long life and good deeds.\" Asked: And who is the worst? He said: \"Whoever has a long life and bad actions.\""
"2778","The previous example is mentioned in this document as well."
"2779","Ibn Muhairiz said: I asked Sayyiduna Abu Juma'ah (RA) who was a Sahabi: Narrate to us such a hadith that you heard from the Messenger of Allah (PBUH). He said: Listen! I am narrating to you a very good hadith. We had lunch with the Messenger of Allah, may Allah bless him and grant him peace. Sayyiduna Abu Ubaidah bin Al-Jarrah was also with us. He said: O Messenger of Allah! Can anyone be better than us? We became Muslims, did Jihad with you? He said: \"Yes (better than you) are those who will come after you and confirm me even though they have not seen me.\""
"2780","On the authority of Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Masoud, the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: \"It is very bad for one of you to say that I have forgotten such and such a verse, rather (it should be said) that it has been forgotten and continue reciting the Holy Qur'an, because it is faster than the running away of a camel from the hearts of men.\""
"2781","Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Masoud (RA) said: The Messenger of Allah (PBUH) said: \"None of you should ever say that I am better than Yunus bin Mata (Peace be upon him).\""
"2782","Sayyiduna Abu Musa Ash'ari (RA) said: The Messenger of Allah (PBUH) said: \"It is obligatory on every Muslim to give charity.\" The Companions said: O Messenger of Allah! If someone can't afford it or can't give charity? He said: \"Then earn with your own hands and eat from that income and give charity.\" The narrator said: Even if he does not give charity? He said: \"Then he should help a needy person\". He said: \"Let him command a good thing.\" He said: What if he can't do even this? He said: \"Respite from bad deeds, this is his charity.\""
"2783","Sayyiduna Abu Hind Dari, may Allah be pleased with him, narrated that he heard the Messenger of Allah, may God bless him and grant him peace, say: \"Whoever takes the position of hypocrisy and hypocrisy, Allah will treat him with the same hypocrisy and hypocrisy on the Day of Resurrection.\" (That is, on the Day of Resurrection, his deeds will be revealed to the creatures and his hypocrisy will be heard by the people.)"
"2784","Sayyidna Ka'b bin Malik (RA) said: The Messenger of Allah (PBUH) said: \"The example of a believer is like the first branch of a tree that has sprouted, which the wind blows, sometimes it falls and sometimes it straightens it until it dies (i.e. dries up), and the example of a disbeliever is like a cypress tree that stands upright on its root, nothing bends it, and finally in one gust it is uprooted.\" Gets up.” Imam al-Darmi (may Allah have mercy on him) said: \"Khama\" means weak."
"2785","Sayyiduna Hakeem bin Hizam, may Allah be pleased with him, said: I asked the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, for something. And he who takes it greedily will not be blessed with wealth, his condition will be like that of a person who eats but is not satisfied, and the upper hand is better than the lower hand.” (i.e. the giving hand is better than the receiving hand)."
"2786","Sayyiduna Mughira bin Shuba (RA) said: The Messenger of Allah (SAW) forbade burying girls alive, disobeying their mothers, not paying their obligatory rights, and taking other people's wealth illegally, talking frivolously, asking too many questions, and wasting wealth."
"2787","It was narrated from Sayyidna Thawban (RA) that the Messenger of Allah (PBUH) said: \"Indeed, I fear the Imams who lead my Ummah astray.\""
"2788","It was narrated from Sayyiduna Jabir that the Messenger of Allah, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: \"A man should help his brother, whether he is an oppressor or an oppressed person. If he is an oppressor, then (his help is) to prevent him from oppressing him, and if he is an oppressed person, (his help is to) help him and deliver him from the clutches of the oppressor.\""
"2789","Sayyiduna Ibn Umar (may Allah be pleased with him) said: The Messenger of Allah, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “Religion is (the name of doing) good.” We said: O Messenger of Allah, may God bless him and grant him peace! Whose goodwill? He (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: \"To Allah, to His Messenger, to His Book, to the rulers of the Muslims and to the common Muslims.\""
"2790","Sayyidna Abdullah bin Masoud (RA) said: The Messenger of Allah (PBUH) said to us: \"Islam began with poverty and then it will become poor as it began.\" I think Hafs said: So be happy for the poor, it was said: Who are the poor? Said: People from tribes (poor and travelers)."
"2791","It was narrated on the authority of Sayyidna Ubada bin Samit (may Allah be pleased with him) that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: \"He who loves to meet Allah, Allah loves to meet him, and he who does not like to meet Allah, Allah does not like to meet him.\" Sayyida Aisha (may Allah be pleased with her) or one of the wives of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: We do not like to die either? The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: \"This meeting does not mean death, but the point is that when the time of death comes for a believer, he is given the good news of Allah's pleasure and his honor and status here. At that time, nothing is dearer to a believer than what is in front of him (to meet Allah, His pleasure and attain Paradise), so he becomes desirous of meeting Allah, and Allah also likes his meeting. And when When the time of the disbeliever's death approaches, he is informed of Allah's punishment and his punishment. At that time, nothing is more unpleasant in his heart than what is ahead of him, so he dislikes meeting Allah, so Allah also dislikes meeting him."
"2792","Sayyiduna Abu Huraira (RA) said: The Messenger of Allah (PBUH) said: \"Allah will say on the Day of Resurrection: Where are those who loved each other for My greatness and majesty? Today I will place them under My shadow on the Day when there is no shadow but My shadow.\""
"2793","Sayyidina Abu Huraira (RA) said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (PBUH) saying: \"None of you should wish for death. If he is good, he may do more good, and if he is bad, he may repent.\""
"2794","On the authority of Sayyiduna Anas, the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: \"I and Qayamat have been sent like these two.\" Wahib bin Jarir pointed to the word and the middle finger."
"2795","Bahz bin Hakim narrated from his father, he narrated from his grandfather: I heard the Messenger of Allah, may God bless him and grant him peace, say: \"You have completed seventy nations, you are the last nation and the most honored and honorable in the sight of Allah.\""
"2796","It was narrated from Sayyiduna Abu Huraira that the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, inquired: \"Where is such and such a person?\" One of the people present mentioned him with bad words that he is like this, the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: \"Didn't he appear in Badr?\" He said: Indeed, they participated. He said: \"Allah was aware of the conditions of the people of Badr and said: Do as you wish, I have forgiven you.\""
"2797","On the authority of Sayyidina Abu Saeed Al-Khudri, may Allah be pleased with him, the Messenger of Allah, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: \"If Allah, the Exalted, withholds rain from my ummah for ten years, and then rains, a group of my ummah will become disbelievers because of this and they will say: This is because of the glorious star.\" \n It is said that Majdah is a constellation called Dabaran. (During the period of Jahiliyyah, the Arabs believed that it rains because of Majidh)."
"2798","Ayyad bin Ghatif said: We went to visit Sayyiduna Abu Ubaidah bin Jarrah, may Allah be pleased with him, and he said: I heard from the Messenger of Allah, may God bless him and grant him peace, that he, may God bless him and grant him peace, used to say: \"The reward of a good deed is ten deeds like it.\""
"2799","On the authority of Sayyidna Ammar, may Allah be pleased with him, the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: \"He who has two faces (two faces) in this world will have two tongues of fire for him on the Day of Resurrection.\""
"2800","Sayyiduna Abu Huraira (RA) said: The Messenger of Allah (PBUH) prayed: \"O Allah! I am a human being, so if I curse, speak ill of, or beat a Muslim, grant him prayers, mercy, and closeness for him so that he may gain closeness to You on the Day of Resurrection.\""
"2801","Sayyiduna Jabir (may Allah be pleased with him) also narrated the same thing, but it has \"zakat wa rahmah\" in it, that is, \"make my bad-mouthing a purification and a mercy for them.\""
"2802","Sayyiduna Abu Dharr said: I heard the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings be upon him, saying: \"I do not like that the mountain of Uhud should be made of gold for me, and on the day I die, I should have even one or half a dinar left from it, except what I save for the creditor.\""
"2803","Sayyidna Ubada bin Qurat (may God be pleased with him) said: Indeed, you commit such things which in your eyes are finer than a hair (i.e. you despise them, do not consider them a great sin), but we used to consider them very dangerous during the time of the Messenger of Allah, may God bless him and grant him peace. \n When this was mentioned to Muhammad bin Sirin, he said: Ubadah spoke the truth, and I believe that hanging Azar is one of the deadly sins."
"2804","Sayyidina Rafi' bin Khadij (RA) said: The Messenger of Allah (PBUH) said: \"Fever is from the steam of Hellfire or because of the excitement of Hellfire, so cool it with water.\""
"2805","Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Amr (may Allah be pleased with him) said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: \"Any Muslim who is afflicted with a physical disease, Allah Almighty orders the angels appointed to protect him to write down the deeds of this servant of mine every day and night, what he used to do (in a state of health) as long as he remains under my bond (disease).\""
"2806","Sayyidna Abdullah bin Masoud (RA) said: I attended the service of the Messenger of Allah (PBUH) and he (PBUH) was suffering from a severe fever. I placed my hand on him (PBUH) and said: O Messenger of Allah! You are suffering from a severe fever, so the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: \"I alone have a fever like two of you.\" Sayyiduna Abdullah Radiyallahu Anhu said: I said: Is it because your reward is also double? He said: \"Yes (it is so) and any Muslim who suffers from a disease or any other problem, then his sins fall off like the leaves fall from a tree.\""
"2807","Sayyiduna Abu Huraira (RA) said: The Messenger of Allah (PBUH) said: \"Whoever sends salutations and blessings on me once, Allah will shower His blessings on him ten times.\""
"2808","Sayyiduna Abu Talha (RA) said: One day when the Prophet (PBUH) came, his face was shining with joy. It was said: O Messenger of Allah! We see a smile of happiness on your face, which we have not seen before? He said: \"Yes, an angel came to me and said to me: O Muhammad! Your Lord says: Are you not satisfied that whoever sends blessings on you once, I will send blessings on him ten times, and whoever greets you (once) I will send peace on him ten times.\" He (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: \"I said: Yes (of course I will be happy).\""
"2809","Sayyidna Abdullah bin Masoud (RA) said: The Messenger of Allah (PBUH) said: \"There are some angels of Allah who roam the earth and bring the greetings of my Ummah to me.\""
"2810","Sayyiduna Jubayr bin Mut'am, may God be pleased with him, said: I heard the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, say: \"I have many names, I am Muhammad, I am Ahmad, my name is Mahi, that through me Allah will destroy disbelief, and I am Hasher that all mankind will be Hasher (on the Day of Resurrection), and I am Aqib (i.e., the Seal of the Prophets) and Aqib is the one after whom there will be no (prophet).\""
"2811","It was narrated on the authority of Sayyiduna Jabir bin Abdullah, that the Messenger of Allah, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: \"O Ka'b bin Ujra! No meat that is forbidden will enter Paradise.\""
"2812","Sayyiduna Suhaib (RA) said: The Messenger of Allah (PBUH) was visiting when he suddenly laughed and said: \"Are you not going to ask me why I laughed?\" The Companions asked: What are you laughing at? He said: \"Every action of a believer is strange (favorable). If he gets something that he likes, he thanks Allah, then it is good for him, that is, he gets a reward, and if something comes to him that he dislikes, he is patient and it is good for him, and no one gets this thing except a believer.\""
"2813","Sayyiduna Anas, may Allah be pleased with him, said: I used to listen to the Messenger of Allah, may God bless him and grant him peace, and I did not know whether these were the words of revelation that were revealed to him, may God bless him and grant him peace, or his own words."
"2814","Amr bin Shuaib narrated from his father, he narrated from his grandfather (Sayyidna Abdullah bin Amr bin Al-Aas, may Allah be pleased with him) that the Messenger of Allah, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: \"(In preaching and exhortation) one does not tell stories except the ruler or the one appointed by the ruler to deliver the sermon, or a hypocrite (so that the people will be impressed by the story-telling and praise him).\" Abdullah bin Amir said: I heard from Amr bin Shuaib: He used to recite the name of the one who causes trouble, so he said: This is what I heard. (It is his honesty that he narrated the hadith exactly as he heard it)."
"2815","Abdul Malik bin Maysara said: I heard from Qurdus, who was a narrator, that a man from the people of Badr informed me that he heard the Messenger of Allah, may God bless him and grant him peace, say: \"If I sit in a council like this, it would be better for me to free four slaves.\" The narrator said: I asked which council was he referring to? He said: At that time, stories were being recited in this assembly. \n Imam al-Darmi, may God have mercy on him, said: The aforementioned companions of the people of Badr are Sayyiduna Ali (may God be pleased with him)."
"2816","Sayyiduna Abu Huraira (RA) reported that the Messenger of Allah (PBUH) said: \"A believer cannot be pierced twice through the same hole.\""
"2817","Sayyiduna Jabir (RA) said: The Messenger of Allah (PBUH) said: \"Do not enter the presence of women whose husbands are absent, because Satan is on the move.\" Sometimes the narrator said: \"Because Satan runs in a man's body as blood (runs).\" The companions said: And in your body too? He said: \"Yes, in my body too, but Allah has helped me in this, so it has become submissive.\""
"2818","Sayyidna Sa'd bin Abi Waqqas (RA) said: The Prophet (PBUH) was asked: Which people have a tough test? He said: \"On the Prophets, then on those who are better than them in rank, then on those who are better after them, and on a man the call comes according to his religion. If he is strong and strict in his religion, then his trouble is also severe and severe, and if his heart is soft and lacking, then the trouble is less on him, and in the same way, the trouble (of sorrow, sickness, poverty, sorrow) will befall the servant.\" As long as he walks on the earth and no sin remains on him.”"
"2819","On the authority of Sayyiduna Umar, may Allah be pleased with him, the Messenger of Allah, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: \"Do not raise me above my rank, as the Christians raised Isa Ibn Maryam above their rank, (rather, this is the same about me). Say: I am the servant and messenger of Allah.\""
"2820","Sayyidina Abu Huraira (RA) said: I heard from the Prophet (PBUH), he (PBUH) used to say: \"Indeed Allah divided mercy into one hundred parts, kept ninety-nine parts for Himself and sent one part to the earth, so from this part the creatures show mercy to each other, even a mare removes her hoof from her foal for fear that the foal may not be hurt.\""
"2821","Sayyiduna Ibn Abbas (may Allah be pleased with him) narrated from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) that he (may Allah’s prayers and peace be upon him) narrates from his Lord, the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: “Your Lord is Most Merciful, so whoever intended a good deed, but was unable to carry it out, a complete good deed is written for him. Even more good deeds are written down, and whoever intends to do evil and does not do it, one good deed will be written for him, and if he acts after the intention, then only one evil will be written down, Allah will erase it too, and there will be no perishing or perishing with Allah except the one who falls into destruction himself (i.e., the one whose destiny is destruction and destruction, only he will perish)."
"2822","Sayyiduna Abu Dharr said: I said: O Messenger of Allah! A person loves a nation but cannot act like them? The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: \"O Abu Dharr! You will be with the one whom you love\", I then said: I love Allah and His Messenger? He said: \"You will be with the one you love.\""
"2823","On the authority of Sayyiduna Abu Dharr, the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) narrated from his Lord and said: \"Allah said: O man! As long as you keep calling on Me and hope (good) in Me, I will forgive your previous sins. O man! If you come to Me with the sins of the whole earth, I will also meet you with forgiveness on the earth, provided that you do not associate anyone with Me, O son of Adam! If If you commit so many sins that your sins touch the height of the sky, then you ask for forgiveness from me, even then I will forgive you and I will not care about anything."
"2824","Sayyidna Nawas bin Simaan (RA) said: I asked the Messenger of Allah (PBUH) about good and bad (sin), and he (PBUH) said: \"Goodness is the name of good conduct, and sin is that which strikes the heart and makes it unpleasant for people to know about it.\""
"2825","The above mentioned hadith is narrated from Sayyidna Nawas bin Simaan (RA)."
"2826","Sayyiduna Abu Dharr, may Allah be pleased with him, said: The Messenger of Allah, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: \"Fear Allah wherever you are, and do good after the evil is done, which will wipe out the evil, and treat people with good manners.\""
"2827","Sayyiduna Abu Huraira (RA) said: The Messenger of Allah (PBUH) said: \"The most perfect of faith are those who have the best morals among Muslims.\""
"2828","It was narrated on the authority of Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Mughfil, may Allah be pleased with him, that the Messenger of Allah, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: \"Indeed, Allah loves gentleness, and whatever He bestows on gentleness, He does not bestow on harshness.\""
"2829","Sayyida Aisha (may Allah be pleased with her) said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: \"Indeed, Allah loves gentleness in everything.\""
"2830","Sayyiduna Abu Huraira (may Allah be pleased with him) said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: \"Whoever I take away two beloved ones (eyes) and he is patient and seeks reward, I will not agree to any reward for him except Paradise.\""
"2831","Ubaidullah bin Ziyad came to visit Sayyidna Muaqal bin Yasar (RA) during the illness in which he died. Sayyidna Muqal (RA) said: I am narrating to you a hadith that I heard from the Messenger of Allah (PBUH), and if I had known that I still had life left, I would not have narrated it. If he dies betraying the rights of his subjects, then Allah will forbid Paradise for him."
"2832","Sayyiduna Awf bin Malik Ashjajai (may Allah be pleased with him) said: I heard the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings be upon him, say: \"The best of your rulers are those whom you love and they love you, you pray for them and they pray for you, and your worst rulers are those whom you dislike and they dislike you, you curse them and they curse you.\" We said: O Messenger of Allah! Shall we not rebel against them by breaking their allegiance? The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: \"No, as long as they continue to establish prayer among you, but when someone sees a ruler committing a sin, do not withdraw his hands from knowing that he is evil and obeying him.\" The narrator of this hadith, Abd al-Rahman bin Jabir, said: I said to Zareeq bin Hayyan: O Abu al-Muqadam! By Allah, did you hear this hadith from Muslim bin Quraza? On hearing this, Zuraiq knelt down on his knees and faced the Qiblah and said: By Allah, I heard this hadith from Muslim bin Qarza, he used to say that my uncle Sayyiduna Awf bin Malik Ashjaji, may God be pleased with him, said, I heard this hadith narrated by the Messenger of Allah, may God bless him and grant him peace."
"2833","Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Amr bin Al-Aas (RA) said: The Prophet (PBUH) was asked about the Trumpet, and he (PBUH) said: \"It is a conch that will be blown.\""
"2834","Sayyiduna Abu Huraira (RA) said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (PBUH) saying: \"(On the Day of Resurrection) Allah will take the earth in His fist and wrap the sky in His right hand, then He will say: Today I am the only king. Where are the kings of the world (today)?\""
"2835","It is narrated from Sayyiduna Ibn Mas'ud (RA) that the Prophet (PBUH) was asked what is meant by Maqam Mahmud. The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: “This is the day when Allah will shine on his chair and it will make a sound like sitting on a new couch (palan), it will be because of its narrowness even though the width of this chair is as wide as between the earth and the sky. Clothe my Khalil, so two fine garments of Paradise will be brought, then after them I will be clothed, then I will stand at the right hand of Allah (Jal Jalala) and this is the place (Mahmoud) that will be envied by those who come after me.”"
"2836","Sayyiduna Abu Huraira (RA) reported that the people asked the Prophet (PBUH): Will we be able to see our Lord on the Day of Judgment? The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: \"Do you doubt seeing the moon on the fourteenth when there is no cloud near it?\" The Companions said: Not at all, O Messenger of Allah! Then the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) asked: \"And do you have any doubts about seeing the sun when there is no cloud near it?\" He said: No, O Messenger of Allah! He (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: \"Surely you will see the Lord Almighty in the same way.\""
"2837","Sayyiduna Ibn Abbas, may God be pleased with him, said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said while giving a sermon: \"People! Surely you will be raised in the Hour with bare feet, naked bodies, and uncircumcised.\" Then he, may God bless him and grant him peace, recited this verse: . . . . .﴾» (Al-Anbiyaa: 104/21) Translation: As We created the first time, We will return (i.e. raise again) This is a promise from Us which We will continue to fulfill."
"2838","Sayyiduna Abu Huraira (RA) said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (PBUH) saying: “When Allah gathers His servants in a land, a caller will call out: Every nation whom they used to worship should follow Him. They will say: We are waiting for our God. Allah will say: Do you recognize Him? They will say: If you tell us, then you will recognize your Lord. Then Allah will open His legs for them and they will prostrate themselves. This is what Allah Ta'ala has said in this verse: . . . . .﴾» (Al-Qalam: 42/68) Translation: On the day when the legs will be opened and they will be called for prostration, they will not be able to prostrate. \n The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings be upon him, said: \"Every hypocrite will remain standing and will not be able to prostrate, then the believers will be sent to Paradise.\""
"2839","Sayyiduna Uqba bin Amir Jahni (RA) said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (PBUH) saying: \"When Allah, the Exalted, gathers all the previous people (on the Day of Resurrection) and judges between them and is finished with the judgments, the believers will say: Who among us will intercede with our Lord? Let us go to Adam (peace be upon him), because Allah created him with His own hand and spoke to him, so he came to Adam (peace be upon him).\" They will come and say: Intercede for us with our Lord. Adam (peace be upon him) will say: You go to Noah (peace be upon him), he will come to Noah (peace be upon him), he will guide them to Ibrahim (peace be upon him), people will come to Abraham (peace be upon him) and he will guide them to Moses (peace be upon him), people will come to Moses (peace be upon him) and he will send them to Jesus (peace be upon him). Those people will come to Jesus (peace be upon him) and they will say: I give you the address of Nabi Umi. The Messenger of Allah, may Allah bless him and grant him peace, said: \"People will come to me, Allah will allow me to stand by Him, then (when I stand) a good fragrance will be released from my place that (hardly) anyone has smelled before. I will reach my Lord and He will accept my intercession and fill me with light from the hair of my head to the nails of my feet. Intercede for us, then arise and intercede for us with your Lord, for it was you who led us astray.\" The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: \"Then he will stand up and there will be so much stench from his place that hardly anyone has ever smelled before, then he will be driven to hell, then the devil will say: \"Waqal al-Shaytaan for what is the matter...\" (Ibrahim: 22/14), Translation: When the decision is made, Satan will say: Allah promised you the truth and I did against what I had promised. I did not pressure you, but I called you and you accepted my word. Can you give it) .... etc."
